{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history","id":1516811,"title":"Wraith Dark Ages History","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-30T11:42:38-07:00","id":1516811,"title":"Wraith Dark Ages History","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> mentioned the idea of Dark Ages Wraith in the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld\">Magic in the Underworld</a> thread and it got me thinking about what that would entail, historically. I threw together a few thoughts of what I know about that era and I welcome everyone to add more.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Basic Setting Points</b><br /> <br /> A Dark Ages Wraith would necessarily take place between the First and Second Great Maelstroms, which happen because of the sacking of Rome and the Black Plague respectively. If we use the 13th century like other Dark Ages it is close to the end of that era.<br /> <br /> Stygia was sacked during the First Maelstrom and Charon rebuilt it as an Empire. By the 13th century it should be well established, but the cracks should be starting to show.<br /> <br /> The Guilds were still legal and they were rising in power in Stygian society. For most of this era they are not a unified force. They would come together to achieve that full political power until right before the 2nd Maelstrom. That process would already be in the works, though.<br /> <br /> Christianity was becoming more and more prominent in society (hence the Fishers). How prominent depends on where in this stretch of time, but by the end of it they\u2019d established their own Far Shore. The Fisher Rebellion itself happens in the wake of the 2nd Maelstrom, but the foundations would happen well before then.<br /> <br /> Transcendence was still accepted and encouraged and the Far Shores were still promoted as places of healing and Transcendence. It is not clear when the Shining Ones started falling, but Stygia didn\u2019t even look into the matter until the Fisher Rebellion.<br /> <br /> That said, the Ferrymen largely left Stygia after Charon declared himself Emperor. Most people who depart for the Far Shores via Stygia are doing so by other means. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Elephant Missing From the Room: The Tempest</b><br /> <br /> The Third Great Maelstrom in the 1600s is said to have turned the Sunless Sea into the Tempest and permanently separated the Shadowlands from the rest of the Underworld. So what does an Underworld without a Tempest even look like? I don\u2019t know, but we have a few clues:<br /> <br /> Argos existed before the Third Great Maelstrom and it is specifically named after a mythical Greek ship. Presumably some sort of navigation was needed in the Underworld even back in the Dark Ages and it was more sea related than anything else.<br /> <br /> The River of Death has existed since Antiquity, so byways in some form or fashion were still a thing.<br /> <br /> Stygia and the Far Shores were always located on the Sunless Sea, which does not correspond to any kind of real world sea. Or at least much of it doesn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> The Maelstrom was said to have separated the Shadowlands from Stygia, so the two used to be more connected.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Possible Elements to Explore</b><br /> <br /> Charon\u2019s descent - Some of Charon\u2019s edicts are said to have come from his Shadow, though it is unclear which ones. Most of the potentials are yet to come but there should be some subtle indications all is not right for his Psyche.<br /> <br /> The New Far Shores \u2013 The Fishers and other established their own Far Shores, presumably without Shining Ones. There\u2019s a lot to explore in what that means, how they found the space, how quickly they fell, etc.<br /> <br /> Doctrine and Dogma - For a variety of reasons, the Fishers as a group would have a major disconnect with the beliefs they espoused in life. It could be worth exploring the potential crises of faith and how that led to the Fall of so many in the faction.<br /> <br /> Other Dark Kingdoms Swallowed \u2013 It\u2019s not talked about much but there were probably quite a few Dark Kingdoms that spanned Europe before the First Maelstrom. This is likely mostly resolved by the 13th century, but a few holdouts may remain until the 2nd Maelstrom.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T12:27:39-07:00","id":1516813,"title":"","content":"Excellent, I was just about to gather the crumbs of info we have myself.<br /> <br /> Regarding the Tempest, it would be strange to me if the Sunless Sea and Sea of Shadows did not function similarly to how the Tempest functions now: as an overlapping dimension which lies between the Shadowlands and the deeper parts of the Underworld. It's metaphysical role for me is the spacial expression of the soul's journey towards the different ends it could seek - a disconnect from life (and the Skinlands through the lens of the Shadowlands) towards the beyond. As such, I would expect it to be a more visceral realm that is sensitive to the expectations of the traveler before the Maelstroms turned it into the chaos it is - Nihils become the 'Gates to the Underworld' and Argos the skill to navigate the 'tests' of the journey.<br /> <br /> I want to read up a bit before writing more, but thank you for the jumpstart with this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T12:38:25-07:00","id":1516815,"title":"","content":"IIRC, the biggest obstacle to a Dark Ages: Wraith (besides the fact that they'd quit doing Wraith books at that point) was that before ... I want to say around the 1600s ... there weren't really much in the way of Necropoli in the Shadowlands the way there were in the modern game. <br /> <br /> My personal work around for this was that Dark Ages: Wraith would essentially be two different games. <br /> <br /> The first (Dark Ages: Wraith) would've focused on relatively younger restless dead still tied to the Skinlands from between the 6th century and the 13th century &quot;present&quot;, who were largely unaware of Stygia and any of its problems or politics. Instead they are completely focused on their own small forts, castles, towns and cities and surviving day to day existence as restless dead. To them, this is Purgatory, where they have to purge themselves of their sins before being worthy of Heaven, and if they happen to come across Stygian wraiths, those are clearly denizens of Limbo who may wish to drag them down into Hell. This would be a medieval gothic low-fantasy setting, with knights and priests and bandits and what have you, where the people have to occasionally deal with freakish demonic monsters (specters and such) as well as their own moral weaknesses (Shadows). Sort of like Army of Darkness with more psychodrama and less slapstick. And it's a society that would've been entirely swept away when the Great Maelstrom of the Black Plague hit.<br /> <br /> The second (Dark Ages: Stygia) would've been the wraiths of Stygia, primarily Roman era survivors of the First Great Maelstrom who would be a bit more experienced and powerful than your average starting character. This would heavily revolve around Stygian politics and plots, the Guilds and Legions, and all the other baggage that Stygia comes with. Basically, the political aspects of Game of Thrones, HBO's Rome series, and film noir tropes set against an ancient backdrop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T17:02:48-07:00","id":1516839,"title":"","content":"Some key events between the first and second Great Maelstroms for reference<br /> <br /> <br /> 476 \u2013 ~1000<br /> Rebuilding of Stygia with Charon as emperor, senators become Deathlords <sup>1,</sup><sup>2,</sup><sup>3</sup><br /> Departure of the Ferrymen <sup>1,</sup><sup>2,</sup><sup>3</sup><br /> Foundation of the Legions and the Imperial Order of the Sickle <sup>1,</sup><sup>2,</sup><sup>3</sup><br /> Restoration of the Onyx Tower and creation of the Seawall in Stygia <sup>3</sup><br /> Decline of the Shining Ones and rise of the Fishers <sup>2</sup><br /> <br /> ~1000 \u2013 ~1200<br /> <i>First Crusade (1096 \u2013 1099)</i><br /> Treaty of Paradise between Fishers and Charon (tithe in exchange for souls) <sup>2</sup><br /> Adaption of feudal systems, formal creation of the Hierarchy <sup>1,</sup><sup>2,</sup><sup>3</sup><br /> Introduction of Thralldom <sup>2,</sup><sup>4</sup><br /> Proliferation of Renegade enclaves <sup>5</sup><br /> <i>Second Crusade (1145 \u2013 1149)</i><br /> <i>Third Crusade (1189 - 1192)</i><br /> Institution, rise and War of the Guilds <sup>1,</sup><sup>2,</sup><sup>3</sup><br /> Dictum Mortuum<sup>\u2020</sup> <sup>1,</sup><sup>2,</sup><sup>3</sup><br /> Foundation of the <i>Piercers of the Veil</i> in Germany (monastic ghost investigator society) <sup>6</sup><br /> <br /> ~1200 \u2013 1347<sup>\u2020</sup><br /> War of the Guilds (ctd.) <sup>1,2</sup><br /> <i>Fourth, Fifth, Sixth, Seventh Crusades (1202 \u2013 1270)</i><br /> <i>Sack of Constantinople (1204)</i><br /> <i>Albigensian Crusade (1209 \u2013 1229)</i><br /> Foundation of the Shadow Inquisition (1223) <sup>7</sup><br /> <i>Great Famine of 1315 \u2013 1317</i><br /> <i>Hundred Years War (1337 \u2013 1453)</i><br /> <i>Black Death (1347 \u2013 1351)</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Unless definitive dates are given, all years are approximations<br /> <sup>\u2020</sup>Different books place the marked events at slightly different points in time<br /> <sup>1 </sup>Wr20, <sup>2</sup> Wr2e, <sup>3</sup> Hierarchy, <sup>4</sup> Player\u2019s Guide, <sup>5</sup> Renegades, <sup>6</sup> Ghost Hunters, <sup>7</sup> DA: Inquisitor<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T07:39:08-07:00","id":1516889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1516839#post1516839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some key events between the first and second Great Maelstroms for reference<br /> <br /> <br /> 476 \u2013 ~1000<br /> Rebuilding of Stygia with Charon as emperor, senators become Deathlords <sup>1,</sup><sup>2,</sup><sup>3</sup><br /> Departure of the Ferrymen <sup>1,</sup><sup>2,</sup><sup>3</sup><br /> Foundation of the Legions and the Imperial Order of the Sickle <sup>1,</sup><sup>2,</sup><sup>3</sup><br /> Restoration of the Onyx Tower and creation of the Seawall in Stygia <sup>3</sup><br /> Decline of the Shining Ones and rise of the Fishers <sup>2</sup><br /> <br /> ~1000 \u2013 ~1200<br /> <i>First Crusade (1096 \u2013 1099)</i><br /> Treaty of Paradise between Fishers and Charon (tithe in exchange for souls) <sup>2</sup><br /> Adaption of feudal systems, formal creation of the Hierarchy <sup>1,</sup><sup>2,</sup><sup>3</sup><br /> Introduction of Thralldom <sup>2,</sup><sup>4</sup><br /> Proliferation of Renegade enclaves <sup>5</sup><br /> <i>Second Crusade (1145 \u2013 1149)</i><br /> <i>Third Crusade (1189 - 1192)</i><br /> Institution, rise and War of the Guilds <sup>1,</sup><sup>2,</sup><sup>3</sup><br /> Dictum Mortuum<sup>\u2020</sup> <sup>1,</sup><sup>2,</sup><sup>3</sup><br /> Foundation of the <i>Piercers of the Veil</i> in Germany (monastic ghost investigator society) <sup>6</sup><br /> <br /> ~1200 \u2013 1347<sup>\u2020</sup><br /> War of the Guilds (ctd.) <sup>1,2</sup><br /> <i>Fourth, Fifth, Sixth, Seventh Crusades (1202 \u2013 1270)</i><br /> <i>Sack of Constantinople (1204)</i><br /> <i>Albigensian Crusade (1209 \u2013 1229)</i><br /> Foundation of the Shadow Inquisition (1223) <sup>7</sup><br /> <i>Great Famine of 1315 \u2013 1317</i><br /> <i>Hundred Years War (1337 \u2013 1453)</i><br /> <i>Black Death (1347 \u2013 1351)</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Unless definitive dates are given, all years are approximations<br /> <sup>\u2020</sup>Different books place the marked events at slightly different points in time<br /> <sup>1 </sup>Wr20, <sup>2</sup> Wr2e, <sup>3</sup> Hierarchy, <sup>4</sup> Player\u2019s Guide, <sup>5</sup> Renegades, <sup>6</sup> Ghost Hunters, <sup>7</sup> DA: Inquisitor<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats really helpful, thanks. I assumed the Dictum Mortuum came after the 2nd Maelstrom but it works so much better for a Dark Age setting if it is new law (hundred years counts as new for wraiths). Add that to the elements to explore list. It might even be the most important.<br /> <br /> The other element that jumps out at me is the Albigensian Crusade. The Albigensian beliefs interact particularly badly with the nature of the Underworld (or alternatively, it doesn\u2019t take too much twisting before they become quite Spectral). I don\u2019t think the event itself is enough to be a major setting point, but older wraiths are not going to distinguish between the Albigensian\u2019s and the Fishers. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T08:49:33-07:00","id":1516893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1516889#post1516889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thats really helpful, thanks. I assumed the Dictum Mortuum came after the 2nd Maelstrom but it works so much better for a Dark Age setting if it is new law (hundred years counts as new for wraiths). Add that to the elements to explore list. It might even be the most important.<br /> <br /> The other element that jumps out at me is the Albigensian Crusade. The Albigensian beliefs interact particularly badly with the nature of the Underworld (or alternatively, it doesn\u2019t take too much twisting before they become quite Spectral). I don\u2019t think the event itself is enough to be a major setting point, but older wraiths are not going to distinguish between the Albigensian\u2019s and the Fishers.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, the inclusion of the Albigensian Crusade was rather impulsive, perhaps because it has some relevance in other splats. It may be better to ignore it.<br /> <br /> The Dictum Mortuum is rather difficult to pinpoint, since the books give different points in time:<br /> <br /> Wr1e: end of restoration period<br /> Wr2e: unclear, but implied to be around the foundation of the Hierarchy<br /> Hierarchy: as early as 543 AD, coinciding with the foundation of the Order of the Sickle<br /> Wr20: after the inception of the Guilds<br /> \u200b<br /> I too thought a relatively recent declaration would be more interesting, so I went with the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T09:17:33-07:00","id":1516894,"title":"","content":"Some thought on the Guilds:<br /> <br /> The Guilds started as <i>collegia</i>, a lose umbrella term for occult orders, mystery cults, social societies, or simply interest groups. During the feudal period, new Wraiths brought the concept of guilds with them and found an already compatible framework in the Hierarchy. Charon, ever eager to copy what was happening in the Skinlands, supported the consolidation of <i>collegia</i> into guilds. This is practically identical to the Skinlands history of guilds, where the consolidation and organization happened during the late 11<sup>th</sup> and early 12<sup>th</sup> centuries. By the mid 13<sup>th</sup> century, one could find as many as 100 different guilds in a single large city.<br /> <br /> The ensuing competition and rather ruthless methods of dealing with it are equally mirrored in the War of the Guilds. While not an open war as such, the conflicts between Guilds themselves and non-guild artisans and crafters surely had their share of aggressive absorption, breaking, and political maneuvering. The books already cover some examples in their history sections. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> said, this is great soil for political intrigue games.<br /> <br /> What that also means however is that during the 13<sup>th</sup> century, the Guild landscape would be very different from the 16 Guilds of the modern era. Instead of being defined by their Arcanoi, it is more likely that Guilds were defined by their trade, and there were much more of them. Some of the Guilds would already have started strong and defined (Artificers), while others were just one among many. It is likely that the different factions within the modern Guilds are the result of mergers or takeovers, such as the fusion of healers, bankers, and moneylenders within the Usurers. A Guild-Wraith would be more specialized in their Arcanoi spread towards a specific task, and it is even possible that some Arcanoi or arts have vanished together with their trade and Guild.<br /> <br /> <br /> Some thoughts on Necropoles:<br /> <br /> With the conception of the Hierarchy and the implementation of feudal structures, it is easy to map the Skinlands roles of medieval society onto the Shadowlands. A large city would have a ruling noble and the presence of guilds and military, which then collects tithe from the land granted to the noble. There are of course going to be obvious differences, as <i>Hierarchy</i> points out, because the only commodity of the Underworld are souls. By and large, the overall infrastructure is very similar though. The value of the land would depend on how many new Wraiths it produces that could be used as recruits, Thralls, or raw material.<br /> <br /> While there would be no Citadels as such, castles would be the logical substitute, especially if they had been subject to siege before and parts of them have crossed the shroud. Monasteries may provide an alternative, but are probably less favored. Some sort of communal shelter is likely, because \u2018regular\u2019 Maelstroms were still as dangerous as they are now, and it factors into the protection a noble can provide to peasants in return for their tithe.<br /> <br /> In the IMO very likely scenario presented by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> that the larger part of the \u2018rural\u2019 Shadowlands populace falls into the category of Wraiths who think themselves in purgatory, I fully expect Hierarchs to play into that and guilt-pressure them into servitude. That would be in direct violation of the Treaty of Paradise, but let\u2019s be honest, the Hierarchs would take the treaty about as seriously as the Dictum Mortuum.<br /> <br /> As for the tithe, it is of course a lot more situational than a regular harvest, but a wider spread of smaller communities would be helpful in finding Drones or alert Legion knights towards a Spectre. <i>Dark Kingdom of Jade</i> runs with that idea and the Way of the Farmer as a dedicated Arcanos, but I think convincing a Wraith reporting and collecting lost souls in need of \u2018purification\u2019 is their duty is easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T08:19:54-07:00","id":1516972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history#post1516811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other Dark Kingdoms Swallowed \u2013 It\u2019s not talked about much but there were probably quite a few Dark Kingdoms that spanned Europe before the First Maelstrom. This is likely mostly resolved by the 13th century, but a few holdouts may remain until the 2nd Maelstrom.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Some thoughts on geopolitics:<br /> <br /> Gauging the extent of the Dark Kingdom of Iron is difficult, since there are not many sources. We know it began in the Shadowlands of the Mediterranean and expanded outwards. Up to the first Great Maelstrom it followed the outlines of the Roman Empire, towards Northern Africa, Central and Eastern Europe, and Britain. Post second Great Maelstrom it tended to follow the spread of Christianity, which is an interesting point in regards to the aftermath of the Fisher Revolt. There is also the important question of the involvement of Stygia and the Fishers in the Crusades, but that warrants an examination on its own.<br /> Geographically, this leaves a few holes on the map; there is room for a possible <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1483797-dark-kingdom-of-ice\">Dark Kingdom of Ice</a> in Scandinavia, Northern Germany, Denmark, Scotland, Iceland, the Shetlands, Faroe Islands, and the modern Baltic Nations.<br /> <br /> Eastwards are the Kievan Rus and the most important force of upheaval at the time, the Mongol Empire. The Golden Horde is invading the whole damn world and with it also parts claimed by Stygia, in the Balkans, Hungary, Byzantine Thrace, Poland, parts of Germany and Austria. They stop and turn at Vienna in 1241 when Ogodei dies and they need to decide whose turn is next.<br /> I recall reading that Wraiths moved with Horde (there was a story about a moving Haunt), but the source eludes me at the moment, and my first impulse would be that in the Shadowlands the Mongol Invasions were used as an expansionist opportunity by the Dark Kingdom of Jade \u2013 someone with more knowledge of eastern Wraith history please correct me on this if I\u2019m wrong. It may also be that the Mongol Empire represented a Dark Kingdom<sup>\u2020</sup> of its own, given that China got the same treatment as the rest of the world. Either way, the invasions would also be a major point of conflict in the Shadowlands.<br /> <br /> Mantaqat Khayal, the middle eastern Shadowlands, have already been subject to the Keening for 600 years in the 13<sup>th</sup> century, so there is little information. One possible option is that Wraiths of the area followed the Muslim conquest to escape the situation, and now exist as an isolated Dark Kingdom in Northwest Africa and the Iberian peninsula. If so, it is one of the old Kingdoms in decline, as the ongoing Reconquista likely parallels expansion of the Dark Kingdom of Iron.<br /> <br /> According to Mummy 2e, Neter-khertet, the Shadowlands of the Dark Kingdom of Sand had already fallen to Stygia, implied to coincide with Roman rule in Egypt at the turn of the millennium. It does not seem like the native Wraiths that had retreated to Amenti attempted to re-seize control after the first Great Maelstrom. But maybe they did and the lands are now contested territory.<br /> <br /> <br /> <sup>\u2020</sup><span style=\"font-size:10px\">The wiki mentions <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erlik\" target=\"_blank\">Erlik</a> Khan in the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Amenti_(Dark_Kingdom)\" target=\"_blank\">Amenti</a> entry, but I\u2019m unable to find further sources on him.</span><br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T17:02:02-07:00","id":1517121,"title":"","content":"Minor updates and corrections:<br /> <br /> - Erlik Khan appears in a Mummy 2e homebrew supplement (<a href=\"https://pdfcookie.com/documents/world-of-darkness-the-mummy-companion-1dvmz0dj7q2y\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy Companion</a>) and may have entered the wiki from there. I like the guy as a possible ruler of a Dark Kingdom, though.<br /> <br /> - <i>Wind from the East</i> sadly doesn't provide much info on Wraiths that traveled with the Horde, aside from those of angry slain foes.<br /> <br /> - I may have confused the story of the moving Haunt with that of a moving <i>caern</i> (one of the wheeled yurts). Still not sure where I got it from, but why not both?<br /> <br /> - The start of the War of Guilds is set at 1096 AD in Vampire: The Dark Ages, which also pushes the Dictum Mortuum closer to the end of the restoration period. That\u2019s a bit early imo, but on the other hand 1096 AD would make a good breakpoint date between the periods, since it is also the start of the first Crusade.<br /> <br /> - Wr1e mentions dedicated Arcanoi for the feudal soul trade, which might just refer to the Arcanoi of the current Guilds but could also mean something specialized like the Way of the Farmer.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-04T15:08:12-07:00","id":1517173,"title":"","content":"Some thoughts on the Crusades:<br /> <br /> Before moving on to the Fishers, I want to first look at the Crusades from the perspective of the Underworld, and mainly from the perspective of Stygia.<br /> While Shadowland conflicts often mirror the conflicts of the Skinlands, I could not find any hints of Charon or the Hierarchy being invested in the various fronts of the Crusades. This could be either an omission because focus was on the larger historical picture, or Stygia managed to hold conflicted territories from before the first Great Maelstrom and did not care much.<br /> However, assuming the existence of additional Dark Kingdoms and Stygia\u2019s starvation for resources after the restoration period, it would be likely that the Legions fought alongside the living armies in Scandinavia, Andalusia, Anatolia and the Levant. It\u2019s also the more interesting variant, imo.<br /> <br /> The Legions did follow the Crusades in either case (undoubtedly along with contingents of Fisher missionaries) to pick up the valuable resources the wars left behind. This resulted in a large influx of Relics and souls, which upon crossing the Shroud eventually distributed themselves into different camps. Some of the Christian and Muslim warriors simply continued their conflict in the Shadowlands, while those realizing themselves not in the respective afterlives they were promised either joined Stygia or the Fishers. Since the latter only presented a viable option for Christians (the Fishers are very much Cross, not Crescent), there is the question whether an analogous faction existed for Muslims. Wr1e at least mentions them \u201cwaiting to be judged at their respective temples\u201d, so there is that. I can imagine quite a few making the pilgrimage to Mecca in search for answers, only to find it impenetrable and ravaged by an eternal Maelstrom and the Keening.<br /> Anyways, this swelled Stygia\u2019s Legions and the Fisher\u2019s ranks, both military and civilian. By the time after the second Great Maelstrom, the Fishers had become the largest faction in Stygia, so they would be well underway to that point in the interim.<br /> <br /> <i>Ashen Knight</i> explores many of the themes a Wraith-Knight might find themselves confronted with, even if they don\u2019t have to drink blood or fear the sunlight. I think much of it could be transported to Wraith, or at least provide an option for tie-ins. It\u2019s certainly an attractive archetype for a player character, with a large enough variety of factions to declare for. Even the Guilds might hire some mercenaries for their own war efforts, and others would pick up the sword again as Renegade robber-knights.<br /> <br /> One thing the Wraith books do not touch on is Jerusalem. There is plenty of information for Vampire and some for Mage, but what was the city like for Wraiths? How many of the Crusaders that fell on the way would have continued their trek in search of salvation? What about the Fishers?<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-05T20:51:35-07:00","id":1517244,"title":"","content":"There really should have been a Dark Ages: Wraith book. Feels like a missed opportunity, especially considering almost every other splat got its own Dark Ages book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter","name":"Doktor von Zwitter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28074_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-05T21:53:27-07:00","id":1517247,"title":"","content":"I believe it was skipped because Wraith had officially been ended several years before Dark Ages began.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T01:09:03-07:00","id":1517251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1517247#post1517247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe it was skipped because Wraith had officially been ended several years before Dark Ages began.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. It also required a lot of work by various long time freelance writers just to get Dark Ages: Fae's single book greenlit, IIRC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T02:57:13-07:00","id":1517258,"title":"","content":"I'm currently also feeling the lack of a <i>Heretics</i> book. Wraith is a very agnostic setting, but Faith is an important component in the mix, especially in the Dark Ages. There is a bit in the <i>Player's Guide</i>, but nothing too in-depth. One thing I've considered but not really developed yet is that splats in DA: Wraith could be tied to a system similar to Roads instead of Guilds. I need to work out if this is compatible with an active Shadow, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T05:28:17-07:00","id":1517266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1517258#post1517258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm currently also feeling the lack of a <i>Heretics</i> book. Wraith is a very agnostic setting, but Faith is an important component in the mix, especially in the Dark Ages. There is a bit in the <i>Player's Guide</i>, but nothing too in-depth. One thing I've considered but not really developed yet is that splats in DA: Wraith could be tied to a system similar to Roads instead of Guilds. I need to work out if this is compatible with an active Shadow, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. A lot about Dark Ages depends on the Fishers and we really don't have much on what they believed or at least professed to. For instance, here's a crucially important question: Did they claim divine authority or not? That is: did they consider themselves an organization of Christians who woke up in the underworld or do them consider themselves to be part of the Church as set up in the Underworld by Christ? Were they just trying to continue their faith as best they could in a new situation, or did they think they had been given a specific way to do that?<br /> <br /> The creeds that pretty much every Christian of the time (and many, many today) used say that Christ descended to the dead and rose again. If some of the oldest Fishers claimed to have been there for that event and been commissioned by Him to spread the Church in the Underworld, that would be plausible to most incoming Christian wraiths. Even if they claimed to be empowered by those who were there, that would still work. In fact, it would be quite notable if they didn't claim that.<br /> <br /> A Dark Age Wratih wouldn't have to say if that was true or not, in fact its probably better if doesn't. But consider the differences in the character of the Fishers actions depending on what they believed. Consider the Fisher Far Shore. If they were just a motley crew of lost Christians, then setting that up (or believing it if someone else set it up) was an act of desperation and a usurpation of forces they did not understand. On the other hand, if they thought they were commissioned by God to advance the Church in the Underworld then it was built with authority and a sense of duty. So much about the time period changes based on this one question.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T05:40:40-07:00","id":1517267,"title":"","content":"I'd strongly recommend presenting them as an extension of the Church into the Underworld. We're still at least a century before Martin Luther triggered the Protestant Revolution; and it wouldn't be until then that the notion of Christian wraiths <i>not</i> thinking of themselves in the context of the Church would have a shot at having any sort of widespread acceptance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T06:04:23-07:00","id":1517269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1517266#post1517266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. A lot about Dark Ages depends on the Fishers and we really don't have much on what they believed or at least professed to. For instance, here's a crucially important question: Did they claim divine authority or not? That is: did they consider themselves an organization of Christians who woke up in the underworld or do them consider themselves to be part of the Church as set up in the Underworld by Christ? Were they just trying to continue their faith as best they could in a new situation, or did they think they had been given a specific way to do that?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1517267#post1517267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd strongly recommend presenting them as an extension of the Church into the Underworld. We're still at least a century before Martin Luther triggered the Protestant Revolution; and it wouldn't be until then that the notion of Christian wraiths <i>not</i> thinking of themselves in the context of the Church would have a shot at having any sort of widespread acceptance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed on both counts. The next thing I want to do is gather the canon info we have and then contrast it with the state of the Church during the time- or rather the different creeds that existed. Eastern Orthodox vs Roman Catholic is by far the largest, but in no way the only divide. I earlier said to ignore the Albigensian Crusades, but the arrival of violently slain Wraiths of a different creed may not be so insignificant to the FIshers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1517266#post1517266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The creeds that pretty much every Christian of the time (and many, many today) used say that Christ descended to the dead and rose again. If some of the oldest Fishers claimed to have been there for that event and been commissioned by Him to spread the Church in the Underworld, that would be plausible to most incoming Christian wraiths. Even if they claimed to be empowered by those who were there, that would still work. In fact, it would be quite notable if they didn't claim that.<br /> <br /> A Dark Age Wratih wouldn't have to say if that was true or not, in fact its probably better if doesn't. But consider the differences in the character of the Fishers actions depending on what they believed. Consider the Fisher Far Shore. If they were just a motley crew of lost Christians, then setting that up (or believing it if someone else set it up) was an act of desperation and a usurpation of forces they did not understand. On the other hand, if they thought they were commissioned by God to advance the Church in the Underworld then it was built with authority and a sense of duty. So much about the time period changes based on this one question.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI fully believe the Fisher Paradise was not set up as a scam, but with the best intentions. At least initially. When it had to become obvious after a certain time and population threshold that vice, temptations, and sin very much still existed and their Paradise was Limbo at best, there must have been an immense pressure on the Fishers to save the situation: Roleplaying the mythology to force the Transcendence that must surely happen once the afterlife is what it should be according to dogma, and not what they found in the Shadowlands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T08:50:59-07:00","id":1517283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1517269#post1517269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> Agreed on both counts. The next thing I want to do is gather the canon info we have and then contrast it with the state of the Church during the time- or rather the different creeds that existed. Eastern Orthodox vs Roman Catholic is by far the largest, but in no way the only divide. I earlier said to ignore the Albigensian Crusades, but the arrival of violently slain Wraiths of a different creed may not be so insignificant to the FIshers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the Catholic and Orthodox will be the most prominent, and for the purposes of the Underworld, there's not much difference between them. The schism was driven more by politics and language barriers than anything else. That's not to say there aren't theological differences, but those differences aren't likely to matter to the average Christian wraith. The single biggest disagreement that would be widely known involves the primacy of the Pope over the other bishops and patriarchs. Since those are living leaders who decide matters of faith as they pertain to the living, its not likely to matter as much in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> For the rest, it depends on the group and the differences they had with the rest of the Church. The Albigensians, I suspect, are not going to have an easy time. Their beliefs stand in direct contradiction of the Creeds (Apostle's, Nicene, etc.). They directly dispute major elements of the faith that the average Christian is likely to know (the incarnation of Christ, the resurrection of the body, the virgin birth, etc.) Not only that, the Albigensians are going to be rocked much, much harder by the nature of the Underworld than most wraiths. As I recall, their faith claimed that the body was the source of sin and that the soul freed from the body was freed from sin. Given that Albigensian ghosts were spirits who were not freed from sin, they'd have some soul searching to do (no pun intended).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I fully believe the Fisher Paradise was not set up as a scam, but with the best intentions. At least initially. When it had to become obvious after a certain time and population threshold that vice, temptations, and sin very much still existed and their Paradise was Limbo at best, there must have been an immense pressure on the Fishers to save the situation: Roleplaying the mythology to force the Transcendence that must surely happen once the afterlife is what it should be according to dogma, and not what they found in the Shadowlands. </div> </div> </div>I agree. That's a separate question from whether they thought they had been empowered to set up, though. Either origin for the Fishers could set up their Far Shore with the best of intentions. If the Fishers thought they were The Church Suffering* directly set up by Christ during his descent would do it thinking that they were divinely commissioned to do so. If they didn't have that grounding they could either claim to still have the mandates they did in life, or just set it up to follow the teachings they knew as best as possible secure in the faith that would be enough. Any of those three options would be good faith efforts to help wraiths Transcend.<br /> <br /> *The Church Suffering is a Catholic term for the part of the Church currently in Purgatory. The Underworld doesn't map perfectly to Purgatory, but if it isn't a great term for an organization in the Underworld I don't know what is.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T10:42:16-07:00","id":1517292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1517283#post1517283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the Catholic and Orthodox will be the most prominent, and for the purposes of the Underworld, there's not much difference between them. The schism was driven more by politics and language barriers than anything else. That's not to say there aren't theological differences, but those differences aren't likely to matter to the average Christian wraith. The single biggest disagreement that would be widely known involves the primacy of the Pope over the other bishops and patriarchs. Since those are living leaders who decide matters of faith as they pertain to the living, its not likely to matter as much in the Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but that may not be the case for the Fisher's leaders and active missionaries. As a group, they appear to be a lot more ecumenical in that they seem to accept the souls of any creed as long as it isn't too heretical, as with the Albigensians. Your question in the initial post was spot on: how did they manage to transform their worldly doctrine and dogma into a workable version adapted to the situation in the Shadowlands? I suspect the different branches would have different opinions, and their leadership would be more internally fractured than they appear towards the outside. There is enough common ground in the shared key values of Christianity to make it work, but it imo needs a catalyst strong enough to overcome denominational differences.<br /> <br /> A divine mandate would be a very, very strong catalyst, regardless of whether it is actual fact or fiction. If that narrative exists, it could be enough to make it work for so long. But even then it would need some kind of catechesis that is able to convince prince, priest, and pauper to get on a Golden Ship and sail away.<br /> A key figure here, I think, is the 'Archbishop' of the Fishers who represents them in Stygia, and who I assume existed before the second Great Maelstrom. He<sup>\u2020</sup> seems to be in the top spot of the Fishers and would need to be charismatic enough to keep all the sheep in the flock.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><sup>\u2020</sup>Male pronoun because the books use it. I would be fine with a female saint figure too, though.\u200b</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1517283#post1517283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the rest, it depends on the group and the differences they had with the rest of the Church. The Albigensians, I suspect, are not going to have an easy time. Their beliefs stand in direct contradiction of the Creeds (Apostle's, Nicene, etc.). They directly dispute major elements of the faith that the average Christian is likely to know (the incarnation of Christ, the resurrection of the body, the virgin birth, etc.) Not only that, the Albigensians are going to be rocked much, much harder by the nature of the Underworld than most wraiths. As I recall, their faith claimed that the body was the source of sin and that the soul freed from the body was freed from sin. Given that Albigensian ghosts were spirits who were not freed from sin, they'd have some soul searching to do (no pun intended).</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, I absolutely feel like they would be thrown into a big crisis of faith. But they, along with other heretics or heathens, could have a strong enough grudge to make revenge their Passion and be part of an opposing group of the Fishers.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T12:10:09-07:00","id":1517297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1517283#post1517283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Fishers thought they were The Church Suffering* directly set up by Christ during his descent would do it thinking that they were divinely commissioned to do so. If they didn't have that grounding they could either claim to still have the mandates they did in life, or just set it up to follow the teachings they knew as best as possible secure in the faith that would be enough. Any of those three options would be good faith efforts to help wraiths Transcend.<br /> <br /> *The Church Suffering is a Catholic term for the part of the Church currently in Purgatory. The Underworld doesn't map perfectly to Purgatory, but if it isn't a great term for an organization in the Underworld I don't know what is.</div> </div> </div> </div> Didn't mean to skip over this. This is good, the kind of matching doctrine I'm looking for.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T03:37:10-07:00","id":1517468,"title":"","content":"I'm completely drawing a blank on placing the Golden Ship of the Fishers in either mythology or history, assuming it is a relic vessel. The best thing I can come up with is the ark. Does anybody have a better idea?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T03:59:58-07:00","id":1517469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1517468#post1517468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm completely drawing a blank on placing the Golden Ship of the Fishers in either mythology or history, assuming it is a relic vessel. The best thing I can come up with is the ark. Does anybody have a better idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>How about the Argo - it carried the Golden Fleece","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T06:05:16-07:00","id":1517478,"title":"","content":"Ah, I should have been more specific: I'm looking for a ship in Christian mythology or history. A co-opted ship from another mythology is of course an option, but I thought maybe there is something glaringly obvious I'm overlooking. Argo is a bit of an awkward fit; I imagine it played a bigger role in the conception of the Argos Arcanos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T06:25:29-07:00","id":1517484,"title":"","content":"I'd stick to Noah's Ark, even though that's technically Jewish mythology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T07:55:53-07:00","id":1517490,"title":"","content":"Vessels of significance in the New Testament:<br /> <br /> St Peter and St Andrew\u2019s fishing boat. <br /> <br /> Zebedee\u2019s fishing boat. That\u2019s the one St John and St James would have used<br /> <br /> The vessel the Apostles were aboard when they saw Christ walk on water. If it\u2019s not one of the above.<br /> <br /> The vessel Jesus calmed the storm in. If it\u2019s not one of the above. <br /> <br /> The vessel Jesus preached in. If it\u2019s not one of the above.<br /> <br /> The best, though, is the prison ship that was wrecked while carrying St Paul to Rome. It is a good size for transport, it has a relic creating event, and it has good thematic resonance with both the ideal and the fallen elements of the Fishers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T08:27:59-07:00","id":1517494,"title":"","content":"It would be cool to say I pulled that all from memory, but I had to look it up. <br /> <br /> One other advantage of the prison ship is it is much easier to explain how the Fishers got hold of the relic. If the Ark was a relic powerful enough to last thousands of years it would likely already be claimed. If some early Christian ghosts were following around the living Apostles back in the first century, though, they\u2019d be in a position to snap that ship up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T10:52:22-07:00","id":1517503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1517478#post1517478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I should have been more specific: I'm looking for a ship in Christian mythology or history.</div> </div> </div> </div>The boat was a very early Christian symbol. It has been used to represent the Church itself reaching a safe haven with its Christian souls onboard, thus a symbol of safety.<br /> The central seating area of the church is called the Nave which derives from the Latin for Ship.<br /> he mast of the boat itself often formed a cross and thus represented the cross especially in times of persecution when the cross needed to be disguised.<br /> A fishing boat might represent the Kingdom of Christ and his followers. Jesus told his disciples to \u201cfollow me and I will make you fishers of men\u201d.<br /> <br /> The boat embodies the voyage of life, of coming full circle and also the last journey, taking us back to the waters of our beginning. Eric Neumann describes the ship of death \u201cleading us back to the swaying, gliding somnolent rhythms of earliest childhood, of the primordial ocean and the night\u201d.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T10:59:12-07:00","id":1517504,"title":"","content":"This is also the etymology behind the name of the Fishers in Wraith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-10T02:06:13-07:00","id":1517632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1517494#post1517494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be cool to say I pulled that all from memory, but I had to look it up.<br /> <br /> One other advantage of the prison ship is it is much easier to explain how the Fishers got hold of the relic. If the Ark was a relic powerful enough to last thousands of years it would likely already be claimed. If some early Christian ghosts were following around the living Apostles back in the first century, though, they\u2019d be in a position to snap that ship up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooo I love this. It gets bonus points for being reasonably close to Jesus in the timeline, which would make a connection with a divine commission more plausible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T02:31:48-07:00","id":1517862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1516813#post1516813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the Tempest, it would be strange to me if the Sunless Sea and Sea of Shadows did not function similarly to how the Tempest functions now: as an overlapping dimension which lies between the Shadowlands and the deeper parts of the Underworld. It's metaphysical role for me is the spacial expression of the soul's journey towards the different ends it could seek - a disconnect from life (and the Skinlands through the lens of the Shadowlands) towards the beyond. As such, I would expect it to be a more visceral realm that is sensitive to the expectations of the traveler before the Maelstroms turned it into the chaos it is - Nihils become the 'Gates to the Underworld' and Argos the skill to navigate the 'tests' of the journey.</div> </div> </div> </div>A bit more on this:<br /> <br /> The books still refer to it as Tempest for history sections pre-Third Great Maelstrom (perhaps for convenience), but it indicates that it still functioned as a separate dimension. I take the descriptions to mean that the 'Gauntlet' between Tempest and Shadowlands used to be a lot weaker, and you could just step into it in some liminal spaces without the use of a Nihil, like a Shallowing in Mage terms. That would satisfy the conditions that Stygia used to be connected to and later severed from the Shadowlands.<br /> <br /> Functionally, I see it working not too differently from a Harrowing, but much milder. The realm would be taking the shape of a transitory landscape or narrative that symbolically reflects a traveling soul's (Dark) Passions, Memories, and so on. It would present a trial to overcome that resembles a stage in their Transcendence they struggle with, or unresolved conflict, etc.<br /> It could be that the Tempest and Shadowlands overlap to such a degree that denizens and structures of either realm are used as the stage for this, allowing for encounters that are tailor-made for a character's narrative. This keeps with the 'speed of story' travel time the Tempest has, too.<br /> <br /> Traveling groups are interesting, because it would be a chance for a character getting an outside perspective on their troubles while experiencing them. I never played a Group Harrowing, but I imagine the dynamic would be similar. And on a side note, Argos would probably still focus on travel, but with a slant towards 'questing' to complement the mechanic.<br /> <br /> I would love to see everybody else's take on a tame Tempest, because I think it's a pretty important element of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T07:42:34-07:00","id":1518241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1517862#post1517862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A bit more on this:<br /> <br /> The books still refer to it as Tempest for history sections pre-Third Great Maelstrom (perhaps for convenience), but it indicates that it still functioned as a separate dimension. I take the descriptions to mean that the 'Gauntlet' between Tempest and Shadowlands used to be a lot weaker, and you could just step into it in some liminal spaces without the use of a Nihil, like a Shallowing in Mage terms. That would satisfy the conditions that Stygia used to be connected to and later severed from the Shadowlands.<br /> <br /> Functionally, I see it working not too differently from a Harrowing, but much milder. The realm would be taking the shape of a transitory landscape or narrative that symbolically reflects a traveling soul's (Dark) Passions, Memories, and so on. It would present a trial to overcome that resembles a stage in their Transcendence they struggle with, or unresolved conflict, etc.<br /> It could be that the Tempest and Shadowlands overlap to such a degree that denizens and structures of either realm are used as the stage for this, allowing for encounters that are tailor-made for a character's narrative. This keeps with the 'speed of story' travel time the Tempest has, too.<br /> <br /> Traveling groups are interesting, because it would be a chance for a character getting an outside perspective on their troubles while experiencing them. I never played a Group Harrowing, but I imagine the dynamic would be similar. And on a side note, Argos would probably still focus on travel, but with a slant towards 'questing' to complement the mechanic.<br /> <br /> I would love to see everybody else's take on a tame Tempest, because I think it's a pretty important element of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that\u2019s a good start. The gentle transition would help maintain the Sea as a different layer while still making it seem as if it was connected to the Shadowlands. I\u2019d probably make the change from the shadowland to byways seamless, and the changeover from byway to [Tempest] similarly smooth. So you could sail to the River of Death from pretty much any Shadowlands body of water, and enter the [Tempest] proper by leaving the River, but going straight from the Shadowlands to the [Tempest] would still take a nihil.<br /> <br /> My watchwords for the modern Tempest are fury and storms. I don\u2019t fully stick to the ocean themes but I do stick to those. For the early Tempest I would instead choose journeys and trials. I\u2019m thinking landmasses and overland journeys are more common.<br /> <br /> That said, I think the Tempest should still be largely nautical in nature. A calmer ocean, but still more ocean than not. It means the harbingers don\u2019t need too much rework. Most of their powers should still work with that setup.<br /> <br /> While the Dark Ages Tempest would not be a constant storm, there should still be the threat of Maelstrom level storms from time to time. In counterpoint there should also be the risk of Doldrums that future eras would never see.<br /> \u200b<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T15:00:08-07:00","id":1518325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1518241#post1518241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I think the Tempest should still be largely nautical in nature. A calmer ocean, but still more ocean than not. It means the harbingers don\u2019t need too much rework. Most of their powers should still work with that setup.<br /> <br /> While the Dark Ages Tempest would not be a constant storm, there should still be the threat of Maelstrom level storms from time to time. In counterpoint there should also be the risk of Doldrums that future eras would never see.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I would make the Tempest landscape fit the biome; for central and eastern Europe a dense forest, sparse mountain, or large steppe could be more appropriate. Arcanoi.. I think I would like those less 'defined', with more variance in expression between practitioners. I'm still thinking about a good solution, but for example, for Argos 1 I had the idea to spend a bit of Corpus to temporarily manifest the memory of a mode of travel. A boat, a horse, a carriage.. something that was familiar in life. Still working on the general concept, though.<br /> <br /> Would you assign a special role to the Shadow while in the Tempest? I thought about it taking the role that Spectres would have in a proper Harrowing, but just giving the Shadow Guide an opening with a trial might also be enough.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T06:21:58-07:00","id":1523546,"title":"","content":"I'm subscribing to this thread because I find it very interesting<br /> Really wished there was a Dark Ages Wraith<br /> <br /> I'm about to embark in an epic chronicle that will give a shot to each game, starting with Inquisitor. So it would be cool to give a shot to a Dark Ages Wraith game eventually<br /> <br /> I have to yet read carefully all your posts, but the idea that itches me the most is that the Empire of the Dead might be seen as a sort of &quot;evil empire is returning&quot; a la Star Wars current stuff. Because it's like a sort of rebuilding empire since the last Maelstrom and it's not as strong as the proper Hierarchy yet.<br /> With an interesting objective of encroaching the diverse Dark Kingdoms of Europe and adjoining territories.<br /> <br /> Way I could see it, while in 1230 the Christendom is pretty much becoming the ruling belief system in Europe, while on the literal other side things are... harder to put to rest.<br /> So there should be some Dark Kingdoms, even if small, that resist still to Charon and his system of handling things.<br /> Even better if this resistance is at the end of their unlives and the Empire is much established, because it could give that scratchy rebel army vibe.<br /> <br /> I'm puzzled as to why you insist on the matter of Cathars as having more trouble to adjust their belief system compared to other Christian beliefs<br /> <br /> Sure it might appear easier for the Catholic Wraith to recontextualize in their belief the Afterlife as the &quot;purgatory&quot;. But not really.<br /> <br /> But I don't see it that much different from the strong believing Cathar to recontextualize it as &quot;yet another fake world of the Evil God&quot; (and maybe also a test of faith from the Good God). But not really too.<br /> <br /> But I don't see it as harder, for as much as I know of the Cathar beliefs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1517283#post1517283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They directly dispute major elements of the faith that the average Christian is likely to know (the incarnation of Christ, the resurrection of the body, the virgin birth, etc.) Not only that, the Albigensians are going to be rocked much, much harder by the nature of the Underworld than most wraiths. As I recall, their faith claimed that the body was the source of sin and that the soul freed from the body was freed from sin. Given that Albigensian ghosts were spirits who were not freed from sin, they'd have some soul searching to do (no pun intended).<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Answering this specifically, the most fervent Cathars believed that the physical world was a &quot;fake world&quot; made by the Evil God and that the &quot;true world&quot; was Haven, the spiritual world of the Good God (I'm simplifying by memory). So the fact that the Underworld could be seen as a trial to Trascend and access to an higher plane of existence isn't in opposition to the Cathars beliefs, in my humble opinion is quite the opposite.<br /> And the push to soul searching is all the better, because the most orthodox Cathars were actively doing that in their life on the fake world. Maybe more than the average medieval person did.<br /> <br /> The real difficulty I see for the truest Cathars in the afterlife is that they'll likely have few or even no Fetters, since they viewed their life on the fake world as a transitional state and something they had to be willing to shed from anyway. Many Cathars would probably not even become Wraiths in death to begin with<br /> <br /> The Albigesian Crusade though, given that it was a genocide (by many historians), would resonate a lot and with a lot of sudden deaths that were unjust and robbed Cathars of completing their soul searching for sure. So that would have created a lot of Wraiths. And we should include also all the not-cathars that were killed alongside them by the Catholics, which might have a change of faith in the afterlife. They could make an interesting and even a rather numerous faction<br /> <br /> Sorry for my Catharian ranting but last summer I found out an acquaintance of mine wrote a thesis about the Cathar Heresy and so we talked a lot about it (I was preparing myself for Inquisitor already), and I wanted to share my perspective regarding this matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-10T07:52:16-07:00","id":1523914,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately, the thread stalled a bit with still plenty of questions left to explore. That may be because there is so little source material to work with.<br /> <br /> For example, the question about an organized group of Muslim souls and their role (if any) in Stygia. The Shadowlands of the Middle East were already ravaged by the Keening, so a Dark Kingdom of their own is very unlikely- except for perhaps remnants in northern Africa and Andalusia. If such a group existed, they did not leave much of a trace in the modern era, but I refuse to believe the Fishers had a monopoly as a powerful religiously motivated group around Stygia during the 13th century. It's possible that they existed as a large Renegade faction within the DK of Iron, but that would have a major impact on the setting which would be hard to ignore for Wraith history further down the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T13:05:16-07:00","id":1524765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1523914#post1523914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, the thread stalled a bit with still plenty of questions left to explore. That may be because there is so little source material to work with.<br /> <br /> For example, the question about an organized group of Muslim souls and their role (if any) in Stygia. The Shadowlands of the Middle East were already ravaged by the Keening, so a Dark Kingdom of their own is very unlikely- except for perhaps remnants in northern Africa and Andalusia. If such a group existed, they did not leave much of a trace in the modern era, but I refuse to believe the Fishers had a monopoly as a powerful religiously motivated group around Stygia during the 13th century. It's possible that they existed as a large Renegade faction within the DK of Iron, but that would have a major impact on the setting which would be hard to ignore for Wraith history further down the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the Keening ever mentioned in any material of the Revised era? Because it might be something that could possibly be ignored if not, like the &quot;Vicissitude is a space parasites thingie&quot; was. While editions up to W5 weren't hard reboots, a lot of stuff from passages to one edition to another was retconned and sometimes in hard ways.<br /> <br /> It's been years since I've read the whole Dark Ages Vampire book, so maybe the Keening was mentioned there too and I don't remember.<br /> <br /> As for the muslim souls, I don't see much problem. If the Keening wasn't a thing, it's still possible a Dark Kingdom of middle-east resists and it is at odds with Stygia. But I am not so well versed in WtO lore as you guys, so I might be missing some Wraith history facts about it<br /> <br /> Also a thing that came to my mind just now: is it possible that one the main vampire players of Costantinople became a wraith after final death? I think it might be neat, maybe as a lore snippet or a hint for a character that isn't explicitely said to be one of them but strongly hinted at (sort of Wraith's Capuchin)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T12:26:14-07:00","id":1524983,"title":"","content":"Another thing that came to my mind and should be considered is that the Cuman\u2013Kipchak Confederation\u200b was quite a big thing in 1230 AD. Their main belief was Tengrism, which could give interesting twist to wraiths with that belief.<br /> I imagine they could be a faction of their own that is besieged from two sides: Dark Kingdom of Iron from the west and the Dark Kingdom of Jade from the east. They will eventually fall, but at the time of DA:W (I want this to be a real thing so much!) I think they should still putting up a fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T04:07:14-07:00","id":1525017,"title":"","content":"I thought about that too, tentatively calling it the Dark Kingdom of Grass. It depends a bit on how you want to play it with the Mongols rolling over it - you could see the latter as an expansion of the DK of Jade, but I think it would be more interesting to have the existing DK remain and even prosper under the mongol conquest. Erlik as the head of that DK still works.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, official sources (primarily <i>Wind From the East</i>) give us little on Wraith involvement. I like to imagine that their societal structure revolves around mobile haunts rather than cities, possibly with similarities to the Bush of Ghosts in terms of geography and the presence of animal spirits.<br /> <br /> There is a lot of room for interesting additions to the Wraith setting, the tricky part for me is fitting it into the existing timeline without breaking things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T11:05:20-08:00","id":1525083,"title":"","content":"Mongolia in Dark Kingdom of Jade is a Conquered Territory<br /> As for Genghis Khan, Yu Huang (or Lung Wang, a Malfean, who diched its demonic great white dragon form and replaced the First Emperor after their secred duel where the Emperor 'won and wrested secrets from its Corpus while it was pinned down' - witch itself present the question, what was Fu Xia's goal who gave Ju-I, a powerful artifact that was able to injure Lung Wang in theory to the Emperor? All and all, Fu Xia basically not just established the paradigm for China but effectively created the Dark Kingdom of Jade that came to rule the Asian underworld of the dead...) probably been prepared to immediately harvest Genghis out of his Caul as fast as possible<br /> IF the Khan even entered the Shadowlands at all - He was associated with the Great Blue Sky/Tengri in life.<br /> Mongolian shamanism revolves around the worship of the Ancestor spirits<br /> So the mongolian Wraiths are... basically non-existant, and were just like the Garou Ancestor spirits or the whole Mongolian Dark Kingdom is (or was) a bit like \u200bKarta, the Dark Kingdom of Clay.<br /> The oral history of Karta's wraiths claims that this pair made Karta their home more than 50,000 years ago... and Karta and the Australian Shadowlands are separated from the other Dark Kingdoms by the Tempest, extremely volatile and hazardous black mass of clouds with a few unreliable and untrustworthy byways<br /> Mongolia culd be similarly 'isolated'<br /> <br /> The Mongol Hordes were called &quot;<i>Storm from the East\u200b</i>&quot;<br /> I could easly see, with the conquerors came their afterlife<br /> This phenomena is actually well documented in WoD; the Great Leap Outward showed the Kuei-jin carry the reach of the Yomi with them and Broken Mirrors (places where the boundaries between the Material World and Yomi Wan have been loosened by massive amounts of mortal suffering) appeared in the affected areas, as far as San Francisco - essentially the Middle Kingdom, spiritually &quot;expanded&quot; and with it the reach of the Dark Kingdom of Jade and the Yama Kings<br /> I mentioned the Yama Kings, because apparently they had some 'contact' with the Mongols. The Hell of Spiked Chains was one of the Yomi Realms around the 12th century ruled by Yama King Dokhor-Khan<br /> The Hell of Spiked Chains was a vast, flat plain inhabited by the souls of mortals that had died in the steppes. Each of these souls were assigned to a tribe at random by the Yama King, who periodically chose one of these tribes as his favoured. All other tribes were stricken of one of their senses (or limbs) and had to obey the favoured tribe in all things. If they disobeyed, or one of the Favoured felt like it, they were put to the tortures of the Spiked Chain<br /> The Hell of Spiked Chains, however, did not survive into the Fifth Age. After the creation of the Quincunx, the Kuei-jin attacked the holdings of Dokhor-Khan in the former territories of the Black Tortoise Court, severing him from his input of Tainted Chi, which allowed his rivals, among them Rangda and Tou Mu, to destroy him and add parts of the former Hell to their own territories<br /> <br /> My two cent is this matter, Dokhor-Khan basically created the Hell of Spiked Chains for the souls of the steppes just as like Lung Wang, a Malfean created the Dark Kingdom of Jade (with own Hell- part, withc is so similar to Yomi basically a part of it)<br /> <br /> So in the Dark Ages, with the Mongolian Horde came I think their underworld, Dokhor-Khan's reach expanded, like a great shadow with roaring tempest... and the Western Wraiths probably shat bricks and tired to built a fortress out of it, because the Demonic Horde in the Underwolrd has arrived...<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T14:12:51-08:00","id":1525087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1525083#post1525083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IF the Khan even entered the Shadowlands at all - He was associated with the Great Blue Sky/Tengri in life.<br /> Mongolian shamanism revolves around the worship of the Ancestor spirits<br /> So the mongolian Wraiths are... basically non-existant, and were just like the Garou Ancestor spirits</div> </div> </div> </div> Is this speculation or canon? I'm asking because I don't think having an ancestor religion automatically grants transcendence, I was under the impression Garou dodge the underworld because of their half-spirit nature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1525083#post1525083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hell of Spiked Chains was one of the Yomi Realms around the 12th century ruled by Yama King Dokhor-Khan\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I need a refresher on eastern underworld metaphysics here; I think I remember that the Thousand Hells were separate dimensions from the Yin world, so more akin to the Far Shores in nature. Which would leave the Shadowlands at least theoretically open to be under a different authority, right?<br /> <br /> My working hypothesis at the moment is a Dark Kingdom in central Asia, wedged in between the DK of Iron in the west and the DK of Jade in the east. When the Mongols rolled out westward, they swept over the Skinlands of the region while the Shadowlands remained under control of the existing DK. The question here would be whether the DK of Jade would have taken the opportunity to expand its territory together with the Khan - I'm leaning towards <i>no</i>, because if the existing Dark Kingdom was based on Tengrism it would more be something of an 'internal affair' (and a hefty influx of souls).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T00:20:29-08:00","id":1525107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1525087#post1525087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Is this speculation or canon? I'm asking because I don't think having an ancestor religion automatically grants transcendence, I was under the impression Garou dodge the underworld because of their half-spirit nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is more of a matter of interpretation<br /> BUT<br /> Kindred of the East, Stargazers and Uktena Tribebooks and Past Lives mentions, even if not detailed why and how, <i><b>some</b></i> shamans, Shinto priests, or animists become Ancestor Spirits instead of Wraiths.<br /> Not Transcendece in the Wraith sense (whatever transcendence is really) but re-classification?<br /> The Nushi complicate the metter, a Nushi is a Yin- or Yang-spirit from the spirit worlds. They are similar to Garou's Totem, but can be shared by members of a Wu of Kuei-Jin or other oriental Shen (a collective Asian term for supernatural beings, basically everbody)<br /> To complictae it further, the Mokol\u00e9' Mnesis (and to an extent the Croax) is basically your own little bubble of memopry, where all of your ancestors wait in an amphitheatre like scene; in the first row your two parents, second row, four grand parents, third row, eight great grand parent and so on upt to the distant Lizard Kings silhouettes at the &quot;top&quot; row? You can easly spot a a few very confused Garou ancestor, apis, or anything basically in your familly - depending of your mnesis trait, how far back you can see. Humans. Kinfolk. Animals. Other races.<br /> The racial memory is limited up to the history of a small territory, since clutches are mostly sedentary... but this is the reason why the so-called Wanderers are so valuable between the lizard people: they are Mokol\u00e9 who travel and have contact with different clutches everywhere, sharing memories between their kind and even mating with the local kinflok, avoiding inbreeding and renewing the knowledge of the clutch. And on top of that, they could use the Fetish, Bowl of Mnesis.<br /> The humans who somehow got frisky with a Mokol\u00e9 could end up in the Mnesis - not Wraith.<br /> (And the Zhong Lung are quite... well they even have a whole Auspice, the Tung Chun, the warriors and lovers, born in the Spring)<br /> <br /> So the canon example are there for a non-half spirit or non-shapechanger to become an Ancestor<br /> Or even &quot;totem&quot;-like entities to supernaturals (and technically humans too)\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1525087#post1525087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need a refresher on eastern underworld metaphysics here; I think I remember that the Thousand Hells were separate dimensions from the Yin world, so more akin to the Far Shores in nature. Which would leave the Shadowlands at least theoretically open to be under a different authority, right?<br /> (and a hefty influx of souls).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> This is again a bit complicated<br /> Thousand Hells is an artificial spiritual dimension created by the Yama Kings from a combination of the spirit worlds of the Yang World and the Yin World<br /> The Scarlet Path and the Ebon Road are the bridges by which Yomi is connected to the Yang and Yin Worlds, respectively. These areas extend from Yomi but are not entirely part of it.<br /> They are borderlands where the Yama Kings' power isn't quite as absolute as it is in Yomi proper, and fugitives occasionally try to take advantage of this.<br /> The febrile and demon-infested spirit bridge linking Yomi and the Yang World is called the Scarlet Path.<br /> The amount of traffic passing along it between the Thousand Hells and the Western hell of Malfeas makes it one of the most noticeable landmarks in the corruption realm. It has &quot;on ramps&quot; in most of the Yang-aspected kingdoms of the Yomi World; these are marked by heavy traffic, wayposts and occasional defensive encampments. The Path itself stands out from its surroundings by its particular mixture of sickly, web-infested jungle trees and sticky red mud.<br /> Near its terminus in the Yang World, the Scarlet Path branches and twists like the roots of an enormous tree as it blends with the ten thousand realms of the Yang World. Theprimary trunk of the Path feeds directly into the gigantic Western hell called Malfeas.<br /> Myriad smaller branches feed into the Realm of Fighting Spirits, the Realm of Atrocities and the Realm of the Great Abyss. Many tiny alternative paths feed into other realms and zones of the Yang World. A very small minority of them are even said to wind up in such unpolluted realms as Shangri La and the Hollow Earth, but it is widely known that such hopeful tales are merely legend.<br /> The Ebon Road connects Yomi to the Yin World like a smooth black shard of bone; it links the Yomi World to the Dark Kingdoms of the Dead and is the sole means of direct passage between the two. Were it within his power to do so, the Jade Emperor would have destroyed the Ebon Road moments after it was created, but he can no more annihilate the Road than he can calm the winds of the Tempest.<br /> Being so difficult to find, the Path is not often used as a means of travel between Yomi and the Yin World. Only the Yama Kings and their greatest generals, who know the secrets of the dark road intimately, can travel with any regularity, and they're happy with the situation.<br /> Near its end, the Ebon Road divides into smaller twin paths. Should a traveler take the descending fork, she eventually finds herself in the Pit of Salt and Iron ruled by the Yama King Wu Hua, which lies at the foot of the Road in the Yin World proper.<br /> The other path slopes upward and deposits travelers on the slopes of the jagged mountain upon which Ti Yu, the Earth Prison of Ti-tsang Wang, is built. The path is heavily guarded by Yu Huang's servants and &quot;demon jailers,&quot; and before long anyone taking this route stumbles into an impenetrable palisade of heavily armed guards. Leaping from the edge of the Ebon Road after the bifurcation sends the character into the Tempest as well, but the winds are notably weaker by that point, and instead of drifting the traveler falls a great distance while being buffeted by winds and hit by stray objects. After an indeterminate time in free fall (more than a second but less than a lifetime; time moves oddly on the borders of Yomi), the traveler comes to rest somewhere in the bowels of the Labyrinth, and must deal with its perils and pitfalls<br /> <br /> So Yomi is seperate, yes, but connected in a very strange way to the Realms\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> (1000 Hells even details, Yu Huang's hell, the Earth Prison of the Yellow Springs, is an artificial place. It has been constructed from memories, dreams and second-hand accounts, and populated with artificial demons, grafted from Spectres and the worst souls of the Empire. Ti Yu is designed to turn souls into white jade, and to keep the citizenry of the Yellow Springs in line.<br /> It was build by the dead, for the dead, and it houses the dead.<br /> BUT for all intents and purposes, Yu Huang is a Yama King<br /> He is just not in Yomi\u200b)<br /> <br /> Now, as for the souls - the Yama Kings are able to claim your soul if you are a bad boy<br /> This... kind of means anyone, really<br /> For a few examples:<br /> <b>Haha No Fukami</b>, translated as Mother of the Depths, is one of the Yama Kings who holds the title of &quot;Empress of Pearls&quot;, ruling over the Hell of Seven Burning Seas. Although not one of the original Yama Kings, Haha no Fukami was the primal ocean mother during the First Age, but changed to her current duty at the request of the August Personage of Jade. Perhaps the least corrupt of the Yama Kings, <b>she is the punisher of crimes made against or upon the ocean, as well as evil acts involving the abuse of fire or water.</b><br /> <b>Emma-O</b> is the Daimyo Of The Dark in Kakuri, the Night Realm, <b>presiding over the souls of the despised and dishonorable</b><br /> <b>Tou Mu</b> in the Hell of Being Skinned Alive, <b>presiding over the hoarders and abusers of power.<br /> Ravana </b>in Lanka, the Demon City of the Rakshas, <b>presiding over the souls of the violent.</b><br /> <b>Mikaboshi</b> in the Wicked City, <b>presiding over the souls of the corrupted, isolated and anonymous sinners.<br /> Hluh </b>in the Hell of Boiling Oil, <b>presiding over the gluttonous.<br /> Rangda </b>in the Hell of Burrowing Maggots<b>, presiding over the diseased.</b><br /> <b>Wu Hua</b> in the Pit of Salt and Iron, <b>presiding over the souls of traitors.<br /> Tou Shen</b> in the Feverish Hell<b>, presiding over those who profited from smallpox. </b>(not so common sin nowdays)<br /> <b>Hine-Nui-Te-Po</b>, <b>presiding over the souls of those who comitted suicide.</b><br /> <b>Malaveyovo, presiding over cannibals</b> and hungry Same-Bito<br /> <br /> And from \u200bWinds from the East we know, Dokhor-Khan's Hell of Spiked Chains was inhabited by the souls of mortals that had died in the steppes<br /> <br /> It is a bit ironic, technically only &quot;good&quot; people ends up in the Dark Kingdom of Jade, because the sinners? They go in Yomi, by Divine Mandate of the Ministers of Heaven, as per the will of the Ebon Dragon, Scarlet Phoenix and above all, the August Personage in Jade - basically God Almighty itself<br /> <br /> Now again from Winds from the East we know, Dokhor-Khan's Hell of Spiked Chain was annexed, rivals, Dokhor-Khan was destroyed by his rivals among them Rangda and Tou Mu, and they added the parts of the former Hell to their own territories - probbably absorbing his &quot;portfolio&quot; and monopoly on the souls who died on the steppes<br /> <br /> I guess it was up to the divine judges where to send the soul if it was for example, lived on the steppes, was violent and gluttonous, was a traitor, managed to go the Plague and to avoid the humilating death by some disease commited suicide<br /> Thats... basically 6 potential Hell where it could be sent, but only one could have it<br /> Heavenly bureaucracy is complicted<br /> <br /> And again from canon materials we know, the Reach of Yomi could expand exit from the &quot;confines of the Middle Kingdom&quot;, like with the Great Leap Outward in the 20-21 century...<br /> <br /> Anyhow this is just my point of view <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> In the Dark Ages I think when the Mongol Horde came, with them potentially could came Yomi too and their servants<br /> And before that with settlers, traiders...<br /> Just like how when the Weast sent their conquerors, like with Alexander the Great to East or the conquerors to the Americas, the Dark Kingdom of Iron followed... and decimated if not completly destroyed the local Dark Kingdoms and laid claim most of the Western underworld<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 11-06-2023, 03:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T02:26:14-08:00","id":1525110,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the detailed answer, there is a lot to unpack.<br /> <br /> So, a rough timeline for central Asia for the 13th century could possibly look like this:<br /> <br /> 1. Dokhor-Khan utilizes the Mongol Empire to expand his sphere of influence<br /> 2. This would result in a conflict with any Dark Kingdom already present, with the latter eventually having to cede territory. There would be some delay between the expansion in the Skinlands and the corresponding conflict in the Shadowlands. By 1240, the Mongol Empire is already in the Crimea, but this does not necessarily have to mirror the expansion in the Shadowlands.<br /> 3. Sometime later, Dokhor-Khan falls to his rivals. If there is no given date for this, the tail end of the 13th century when Kublai Khan dies and the Empire fractures might be a good point. His rivals could have seen that he over-extended and used this to their advantage.<br /> 4. This internal strife would have been the chance for the Dark Kingdom of Iron to then occupy the weakened territories.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-08T04:59:02-08:00","id":1525203,"title":"","content":"Just for fun, Dragons of the East mentions the <b>Sons of Tengri,</b> a shamanistic Craft and Awakened inheritors of the animist traditions of the Mongols.<br /> Central to the paradigm of the Sons of Tengri is are the gods Tengri, who rules over the sky, and It\u00fcgen, who is the Earth Mother. Beneath them are numerous spirits, both nature spirits and the spirits of the dead. The Sons of Tengri keep rapport to all of them, with a special relation to the spirits of running water.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1525110#post1525110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Dokhor-Khan utilizes the Mongol Empire to expand his sphere of influence</div> </div> </div> </div>This would certanly explain the unsually bitter enmity between the Anda and the Kuei-jin<br /> During the rise of Qin Shihuangdi aka <b>Yu Huang</b>, the Black Tortoise Court allied with several Beast Courts to fight the emperor and his wizard allies.<br /> After the creation of the Quincunx, the Kuei-jin attacked the holdings of Dokhor-Khan in the former territories of the Black Tortoise Court, severing him from his input of Tainted Chi<br /> (To combat tvarious threats and to survive the turning of the Wheel, the Ancestor of the Yellow Emperor Court called for a meeting of all influential Ancestors, which would be referred to as the Council of Dragons. In 1304, the congregation met at the Shaolin monastery near Changan. During the Council, it was declared that the foreigners, particular those strange beings calling themselves Cainites, were to blame for the fall of the August Courts. In response, the Treaty of the Quincunx established a new order, again comprised out of several courts in all directions)<br /> The Anda lived openly in the tribes and when Genghis Khan rose to power. As the Mongol tribes were united, the Anda followed them like a storm, crippling Wan Kuei holdings like the Black Tortoise Court and harassing Cainites in the West<br /> This align with the traditional Yama King vs Kiei-jin conflicts, just the Yama King this time not only used corrupted Kuei-jin (tho' there were numerous akuma in the mongolian ranks) but &quot;western&quot; cainites - to the point the Wan Kuei began a pogrom against the bloodline, and by 1388, no traces could be found of the Anda, BUT It has been rumored, however, that Elder members of the bloodline had merged with the steppes and will emerge during the dawning of the Sixth Age. When Dobrul the Brave rose, the progenitor of the Anda, many Wan Kuei know that the turning of the Wheel has finally begun<br /> It is interesting to note, Dobrul is a 4th Generation childe of Ennoia herself<br /> Buuuuut.... legend says that Dobrul was in life one of the sons of Mother It\u00fcgen, the earth goddess. When It\u00fcgen came under attack by Xia demons (the Wan Kuei), Dobrul was one of her sons who stood guard at her side, waging bloody war against the demon-bandits for days on end. It was he who held the ground as she made her retreat.<br /> So in mongolia, we could se the mix and match, intertwining of several supernatural forces<br /> But all point in to one direction, witch is basically what you described:<br /> Dokhor-Khan used the Anda and corrupted Kuei Jin to use the Mongol Hordes to expand his influence and this triggered such a violent response from the Wan Kuei, he weakned to the point his rivels destroyed them - but in the mean time Black Tortoise Court and Hengeyokai alliance fought against the Emperor... who in turn fought a two front war too, against the Mongol Wraiths and the Wan Kuei<br /> And then the Westerns entered the fray<br /> I guess around this time the Shadowlands became a battlefield - more than usual, especially considering Yu Huang is not a Wraith but a Malfean, Lung Wang (with a demonic white dragon &quot;true form&quot;) with a de facto Yama King status and the Dark Kingdom of Iron is all too familiar with Malfeans... \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 11-08-2023, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T05:02:09-08:00","id":1525245,"title":"","content":"Following this train of thoughts, potentialy on the west there is one more &quot;danger from the East&quot; the Dark Ages Wraiths could encounter - of course if you are not against some heavy corssover<br /> This time the &quot;blame&quot; is on the Salubri, namely <b>Mokur</b><br /> He was originally a simple potter of the J\u014dmon people and Embraced during Saulot's wanderings in the Middle Kingdom<br /> In Japanese history, the J\u014dmon period is the time between c. 14,000 and 300 BC<br /> Bear with me, soon it will make sense, I promise<br /> Originally Emma-O was the guide of the dead for the Ainu peoples of the islands known today as Japan. Revered as a benevolent deity, Emma-O gained great power and took upon himself to punish the wicked and protect the good. This worked well until the modern day inhabitants came, subjugating and decimating the Ainu people. Emma-O was furious and wanted revenge against the Japanese... and they delivered it to him.<br /> The Japanese saw Emma-O as a demonic lord of punishment and partially integrated him into their beliefs. This was enough for Emma-O to gain power and become the demon of punishment they saw him as, feeding his rage and punishing the sinners.<br /> Now here comes the connection!<br /> The Ainu are descedants of the J\u014dmon people.<br /> Thus' follwing the established lore - like how East could 'expand' spiritually, it is not impossible Emma-O, Daimyo Of The Dark, a bona fide Death God gain acces to the West via Mokur<br /> Where he went, Emma-O's shadow potentially could follow him to protect this Ainu-ancestor... or hunt him, because of his Cainite state, to destroy him/free him from this abominable state of existance - dealer's choice<br /> The looming shadow of a Death God - a very Yin Aspected Yama King that is - and his servants could have been terrifying to the Wraiths<br /> Mokur was Diablerized by Etrius in 1525 CE (quite a feat considering he was in the state of Golconda...) but with his Final Death Emma-O lost this possible connection (or at least interest) to the West<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 11-09-2023, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-13T16:00:10-08:00","id":1525411,"title":"","content":"One thing regarding the territorial conquests is that there is a distinct possibility that they were enacted by Fisher crusader Wraiths rather than Charon's Legions. There are several indications for this:<br /> <br /> Some time - actually around the crusades - the Dark Kingdom of Iron's outline started to follow the spread of Christianity instead of the extend of the Roman Republic / Empire as it did before. The Fishers are mentioned to become the strongest faction in Stygia, and that requires a military power at least on par with the Legions. The conquests in return would have seriously bolstered the political influence of the Fishers, even within the Hierarchy - who are more likely to follow power rather than philosophical convictions.<br /> That actually gives a good idea of just how powerful the influence of the Fishers would become until the Revolt, and it did not stop with it. Most notably they were still able to conquer the Dark Kingdoms of the Americas much later, after they had been expelled from Stygia.<br /> <br /> For the setting, I think it is likely that the Shadowlands also mirrored this aspect of medieval Europe in that swathes of the Dark Kingdom of Iron were owned and under jurisdiction by the church, either by concession or conquest. Wr20 even mentions 'Death-Bishops', the ecclesiastic counterpart of the Deathlords, who could have been in control of these dioceses. That provides some interesting set-up for the later years after the Revolt, because while externally the Dark Kingdom of Iron appeared as a bloc, there would be a strong internal divide between 'church and crown'. And at least for some time, Fisher activity would not be solely restricted to the Far Shores.<br /> <br /> Charon had always been more concerned with fighting Oblivion and keeping internal stability rather than aggressive expansion towards other Dark Kingdoms. It would fit that holdings by the Fishers became his after mopping up Heretics rather than conquering them himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-14T00:06:20-08:00","id":1525424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charon had always been more concerned with fighting Oblivion and keeping internal stability rather than aggressive expansion towards other Dark Kingdoms. It would fit that holdings by the Fishers became his after mopping up Heretics rather than conquering them himself.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>That both makes sense and completely reconceptualizes my understanding of the setting period.<br /> Heck, it goes a long way to explaining the incongruence between the Republic style Hierarchy that Charon founded and the dictatorial fascistic one we see in by the Great War. <br /> The rise of the Fishers pushes the concept of divine right and the weak souls are doomed to hell without intervention and may find redemption through the soulforgers of the Artificers, a concept that could be applied to those not &quot;of the faith&quot;. Throw in the Death Bishops as an extra layer of separation, Charon might not have known about the scale of it for a while.<br /> <br /> Actually, would the Mnemoi be considered a High Guild at this point? Their &quot;fall&quot; from grace occurs around the 3rd Great Maelstorm (placed 1605 AD, iirc), so they are still around and active.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-20T14:19:53-08:00","id":1525697,"title":"","content":"I do think that ramping up the Fishers' effect on the setting works well, to a point. I don't think that they can be the driving force behind the expansion of Stygia. If they were that powerful, they would have essentially been a new Dark Kingdom in their own right. It makes them too powerful for what comes next.<br /> <br /> In fact, I don't think we need a driving force behind the expansion of Stygia. While Stygia itself may be controlled by the oldest wraiths, its shadowlands presence follows the newly dead and they follow their skinlands kin. Stygia doesn't need a reason to expand, it needs a reason not to.<br /> <br /> I would draw an important distinction. Stygia didn't follow Christianity intentionally. It followed Christianity because who was there after Rome fell. It may seem like a blurry distinction, but it means that Stygia and the Fishers grew together for a time, but were never truly aligned. That sets up for the future conflict.<br /> <br /> I would not offload the spread of Soulforging onto the Fishers, though. Firstly because soulforging was already tightly bound with Stygian society by this time. Secondly because the Fishers will eventually be &quot;unmasked&quot; as spectral*, and its a profound enough revelation that the Far Shores and the very idea of Transcendence were tarnished as a result. If Soulforging was their thing, it would likely die with them. On the other hand, if they were vocal opponents of soulforging (if only because their members kept getting soulforged) it might push Stygia even further in that direction.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T01:53:53-08:00","id":1525776,"title":"","content":"I was not suggesting &quot;offloading&quot; soul forging on to the Fishers. I was providing a rationalization for why some of these future Heretics could support the single most horrific institution in the Underworld. Which would be necessary for the quasi-integration thing I thought we were aiming for.<br /> <br /> That said, with both the Fishers and the Guilds playing roles in society at large and in public, the basic assumptions shift a bit. It almost feels like the setting is more stable. The Legions might not be the backbone of the Dark Kingdom of Iron. The fact you died of illness might not define who you serve, it might be more &quot;which church do you go to? what's your job?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T03:51:19-08:00","id":1525829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1525697#post1525697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think that ramping up the Fishers' effect on the setting works well, to a point. I don't think that they can be the driving force behind the expansion of Stygia. If they were that powerful, they would have essentially been a new Dark Kingdom in their own right. It makes them too powerful for what comes next.<br /> <br /> In fact, I don't think we need a driving force behind the expansion of Stygia. While Stygia itself may be controlled by the oldest wraiths, its shadowlands presence follows the newly dead and they follow their skinlands kin. Stygia doesn't need a reason to expand, it needs a reason not to.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b\u200bI honestly think it's both, with degrees of either active and passive expansion. For example, I see expansion into a possible Dark Kingdom of Ice around Scandinavia as a mostly passive affair. The Christianization that took root during the 8th through 12th centuries would simply slowly convert the populous in both Skinlands and Shadowlands until the majority of Wraiths were de-facto aligned with Fisher ideology, and by extension, Stygia. On the other hand, places of major conflicts between sides (such as with the Mongol expansion in central Asia, and the Muslim conquest in Anatolia and the Near East) require a more active involvement. Jerusalem in particular is almost certainly a site of conflict.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1525697#post1525697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would draw an important distinction. Stygia didn't follow Christianity intentionally. It followed Christianity because who was there after Rome fell. It may seem like a blurry distinction, but it means that Stygia and the Fishers grew together for a time, but were never truly aligned. That sets up for the future conflict.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this. I should have specified it when I said that Stygian expansion followed Christianity.<br /> <br /> I still think having the Fishers in control of portions of the Shadowlands while nominally being subject to Stygian jurisdiction works well for the setting. It reflects how they established a parallel power structure to the Stygian model, within the same Dark Kingdom. It also increases the importance of the tithe towards Charon as a point of major conflict.<br /> <br /> A question that popped up in relation to this is, how connected were the Fishers with the Skinland Church?<br /> The description of Ghosts in DA:Inquisitor material is rather careful to paint judgement of Wraiths as a case-to-case basis, but there is nothing really on the Fishers themselves. Exploring the relationship between the higher ups of Church and Fishers could be interesting- what if the Church handles the Fishers straight up as a branch that extends into the afterlife? Mix in a Divine Mandate as we previously discussed, and that dynamic gives the Fishers a serious hand in Skinland affairs. While I think the Archbishop would be careful to preserve some degree of independence, there is nothing really stopping him from Embodying into the pope's bedchamber and going &quot;Yo Greg, I have a message from God.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1525697#post1525697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would not offload the spread of Soulforging onto the Fishers, though. Firstly because soulforging was already tightly bound with Stygian society by this time. Secondly because the Fishers will eventually be &quot;unmasked&quot; as spectral*, and its a profound enough revelation that the Far Shores and the very idea of Transcendence were tarnished as a result. If Soulforging was their thing, it would likely die with them. On the other hand, if they were vocal opponents of soulforging (if only because their members kept getting soulforged) it might push Stygia even further in that direction.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1525776#post1525776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was not suggesting &quot;offloading&quot; soul forging on to the Fishers. I was providing a rationalization for why some of these future Heretics could support the single most horrific institution in the Underworld. Which would be necessary for the quasi-integration thing I thought we were aiming for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see Soulforging to be a thing for the Fishers once their Paradise collapses and they start to emulate hell. Before that, it runs too much opposite to their ideology, although there may be exceptions for souls that are judged to be irredeemable. While they hoarded a lot of relics, the materials they needed had to come from somewhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1525776#post1525776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, with both the Fishers and the Guilds playing roles in society at large and in public, the basic assumptions shift a bit. It almost feels like the setting is more stable. The Legions might not be the backbone of the Dark Kingdom of Iron. The fact you died of illness might not define who you serve, it might be more &quot;which church do you go to? what's your job?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>For the time Guilds and Legions existed in parallel, my guess would be that the Legions were more military focused while the civilian branches where more under the control of the Guilds. You can still use Charon's Sorting Hat, it's just that a civilian Wraith would be more tied to a Guild than a Legion in day-to-day business.<br /> That isn't so different to their mortal lives. If you were in the glass-maker guild, your lord could still call you to arms as militia if needed. I imagine a Hierarch could do the same if you happen to fall into their jurisdiction. But in general I agree, there are more layers of allegiance depending on what you do and who you are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T05:29:04-08:00","id":1525835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1525829#post1525829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question that popped up in relation to this is, how connected were the Fishers with the Skinland Church?<br /> The description of Ghosts in DA:Inquisitor material is rather careful to paint judgement of Wraiths as a case-to-case basis, but there is nothing really on the Fishers themselves. Exploring the relationship between the higher ups of Church and Fishers could be interesting- what if the Church handles the Fishers straight up as a branch that extends into the afterlife? Mix in a Divine Mandate as we previously discussed, and that dynamic gives the Fishers a serious hand in Skinland affairs. While I think the Archbishop would be careful to preserve some degree of independence, there is nothing really stopping him from Embodying into the pope's bedchamber and going &quot;Yo Greg, I have a message from God.&quot;\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that depends entirely on how hypocritical you want to portray the Skin land Church. The Biblical injunction about not tolerating witches is actually a prohibition against engaging in necromancy \u2014 that is, trafficking with the dead. It's basically the Dictum Mortuus, but enforced from the Skinlands side. <br /> <br /> After a quick search through <b>Dark Ages: Inquisitor</b>, I'm not finding anything to contradict this. So I suspect that the Fishers might view themselves as a continuation of the Church into the Afterlife; but they tend not to have any actual dealings with the Skinlands Church. That is, the don't take orders from Rome, nor do they presume to give orders <i>to </i>Rome. And the Church generally knows very little of the Fishers; as they're generally so ignorant of the goings on in the Afterlife that they'd likely be surprised that there's a whole society of the dead existing in parallel to the living. <br /> <br /> There would be exceptions, of course. A dirty secret of the Fishers' Paradise, after all, is that they're creating artificial angels there by soul-crafting wraiths to resemble angels. And I could see the occasional pseudo-angel visiting the clergy in the Skinlands and attempting to pass itself off as an actual messenger of God. But such incidents should be the exception, as the pseudo-angels of the Fishers' Paradise aren't known in this time period. <br /> <br /> More generally, I see no more reason to link the Fishers to the Skinlands Church than there is to link Stygia to the civil powers in the Skinlands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T06:57:37-08:00","id":1526060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1525829#post1525829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> I still think having the Fishers in control of portions of the Shadowlands while nominally being subject to Stygian jurisdiction works well for the setting. It reflects how they established a parallel power structure to the Stygian model, within the same Dark Kingdom. It also increases the importance of the tithe towards Charon as a point of major conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div>That part makes sense. This particular time in Stygian history lends itself to the various powers within the Dark Kingdom. I imagine the Legions would sometimes fall into similar patterns, though given their ties to Stygia proper this ended up being less of a problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1525835#post1525835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that depends entirely on how hypocritical you want to portray the Skin land Church. The Biblical injunction about not tolerating witches is actually a prohibition against engaging in necromancy \u2014 that is, trafficking with the dead. It's basically the Dictum Mortuus, but enforced from the Skinlands side.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a bit more complicated than that. The Church encouraged people to ask the dead to pray for them, and there's a long history of saintly apparitions. The prohibitions are against trafficking with the dead by other means and for other reasons. Not only are the means suspect, but few people have any ability to tell the difference between a ghost and a demon.<br /> <br /> If an honest Fisher materialized to one of the living, that person could agree to pray for the Fisher and could ask the Fisher to pray for him. If the living person was a priest he could probably also see to a proper burial or blessing or other intrinsically good acts. Outside of that there's not much legitimate interaction.<br /> <br /> Thinking on it, that's quite a lot really. If done right that could generate quite a bit of Memoriam.<br /> <br /> A dishonest Fisher could show up and claim to be a saint, including one no one has heard of before, and that would work to a point. Saints did (and do) command a lot of respect within the Church. They don't command any actual authority though, and they attract a lot of attention and scrutiny.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T15:15:51-08:00","id":1526084,"title":"","content":"Saints and visions of them is what gave me some confidence in the idea that the connections between Fishers and Church would be stronger than that between secular Wraiths and Skinland institutions when the question popped up for me. Sure, necromancy was forbidden, but as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> said, there were some exceptions - if the ghost was a soul in purgatory seeking aid from their living relatives, it was absolutely valid to help it with its transcendence. Remnants of folk religions and traditions that were tolerated or integrated into a Christian framework left room for Mediums in the commoner social stratum, too, such as some of the Benandanti in WOD. Also on the point of Saints, it always struck me that holy relics (not Shadowland Relics, the Skinland thing) would ironically make great foci for necromancy, and I would wager at least some of them are Fetter items. Relics of saints were widely employed to do all kinds of miraculous things, which might be attributed to Arcanoi of an attracted Wraith.<br /> <br /> I was being hyperbole in my previous comment, but consider: Assuming the Archbishop believed that what he was doing was a direct order of God, and also that the Church represented God's will in the Skinlands, I have a hard time believing that he would not try to convey this to the Church in some way (maybe to a secret order <i>within </i>the Church?). Unless the Fisher's doctrine expressively forbids it, it would be almost mandatory. Minor point to consider here, the Fishers predate the Dictum Mortuum- another option could be that the relationship used to be tighter in the post-roman period and then deteriorated. On the other hand, the idea of purgatory as a 'physical' place rather than an abstract state of the soul only really gained traction in the 12th century. There are certainly pieces that would fit for either option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-14T12:26:10-08:00","id":1526812,"title":"","content":"I've been debating this with myself for a while now and thought I would bring it to the forums where others could weigh in, because I can't really make up my mind about it: earlier in this thread I mentioned the idea to port over <i>DA:Vampire</i> Roads to a Dark Ages Wraith.<br /> <br /> One reason is because I enjoy this system of course, but there are a few others:<br /> <br /> - Transcendence seems to be much more in reach for the average Wraith than in the modern setting, and it is more likely to become the concrete goal of a character rather than a 'side effect' of resolving their Fetters. Roads could be way to reflect this mechanically- perhaps taking the place of Angst as an inverted score. I'm also feeling like it might tie into the [Tempest] in some way.<br /> <br /> - Moral and ethical frameworks were different from today's, and perhaps more rigid. Religions are the big one with something like the Road of Heaven covering it, but the other Roads are also covering a broad spectrum of alternative outlooks that fit into the time.<br /> <br /> - Supplements for the Roads are already there and conversion seems to be easy if you transpose some keywords.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand, there are good reasons against changing the system that way:<br /> <br /> - Personal ethics and morals are already covered by Passions and Dark Passions. Introduction of another system might be superfluous and over-complicate an already rather complex system.<br /> <br /> - Something like a Road system could rob the Shadow Guide of agency.<br /> <br /> <br /> Do you think the different times warrant a different way towards Transcendence? Maybe not with Roads, but something else? Or should the W20 system be ok without alterations?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T02:16:33-08:00","id":1526839,"title":"","content":"It depends on <i><b>how</b></i> you want to port over the Roads.<br /> You could do them as merits that interact with appropriate subsystems (Passions, Dark Passions, the Spite, the Shadow, etc) rather than Virtues and Humanity. Wraiths don't have those traits, so working off the equivalents they do have is significantly less work and lessens Issue 1. <br /> <br /> I'd argue that done correctly, the &quot;Sins of the Road&quot; could be a useful Tool for the Shadow Guide. Even if it is just as Dark Passion that the Shadow gets for free with the merit, that is a nice extra tool.<br /> <br /> I would request that such &quot;Roads&quot; not ACTUALLY directly impact Transcendence. That has ...unpleasant implications around real world religions, especially in the modern day. <br /> (&quot;Sorry Seamus, but as a 21st centaury Catholic, you don't have the right mindset to reach Transcendence/Heaven because the values are too far removed from the Dark Ages&quot;)<br /> <br /> The changes to the Hierarchy of Sins would be the big tickets though; what sins do Wraiths have as part of their template? <br /> It is all well and good to claim that violating the code gives the Shadow the/an appropriate Dark Passion roll, but we still need a baseline.<br /> <br /> Likewise, what would the benefits of a Road be for a Wraith? No Virtues, but I suppose a Passion could be generated for each of them. Still, non-Road Wraiths have Passions, so what makes them special? Can they use them in other ways, like resisting/fighting Harrowings. What do they look like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T03:41:27-08:00","id":1526844,"title":"","content":"I could definitely see addressing the topics that made you think of porting Roads over. But I wouldn't actually do it by porting Roads over. Instead, I'd make a bigger deal of the Eidolon Background: the wraith's \u201chigher self\u201d, represented in-game by a pool of dice that get used up boosting rolls to resist the Shadow, and are refreshed every session. The <b>Shadow Player's Guide</b> has a chapter on the Eidolon, which goes into more ways to detail and use the Eidolon. That chapter suggests that Eidolons don't have Archetypes of their own, but instead represent \u201can idealized actualization \u2014 or in some cases, a true indication \u2014 of the wraith's Nature, which a fortunate wraith may glimpse in a dream or vision.\u201d Though I could see introducing an alternate system that handles it differently, giving the Eidolon an Archetype of its own.<br /> <br /> In fact, <b>Dark Reflections: Spectres</b> has a section in it on Psyches, which serves as a sort of \u201chigher self\u201d for a Spectre and is handled mechanically as an inversion of the rules for the Shadow (it's played by a Psycheguide, has its own Archetype, a Composure score, Passions, and Fronds that serve as an inverse of a Shadow's Thorns.) Some of most of these elements could be adapted for use with a wraith's Eidolon for those groups who want their characters to have \u201cshoulder angels\u201d on par with the \u201cshoulder devil\u201d Shadows that every wraith must contend with. The Eidolon Archetype could be one of the Psyche Archetypes from <b>Dark Reflections</b>, or they might be something inspired by <b>Vampire</b>'s Roads. Composure would equal the Background rating for Eidolon. You could spend additional Freebie/Experience Points to acquire Fronds. The only thing I'd leave out would be Eidolon Passions, as the description of Eidolons highlights that their essence of calmness and Composure is antithetical to the notion of Passions; though even there, you might adapt the mechanics of Passions to describe the Eidolon's Ideals.<br /> <br /> I use the term \u201cIdeals\u201d to distinguish them from a vampire's Virtues; but the concept is similar. Indeed, Fishers in particular would likely feature Ideals based on the Catholic Virtues: Faith, Hope, Charity, Temperance, Justice, Prudence, and Fortitude. That said, I wouldn't want to bake that in as a <i>requirement</i>; just include them as <i>suggestions</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-15-2023, 08:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T07:15:24-08:00","id":1526846,"title":"","content":"The Hierarchy declared that Transcendence is a myth in response to finding out about the fall of the Shining ones. Both the declaration and the relative acceptance of it implies that there wasn't much experience with Transcendence outside those islands. So if there were special philosophies that actually led to Transcendence, they were likely things learned once Wraiths reached those shores and not something the typical Wraith would experience otherwise.<br /> <br /> The other possibility, and one that I like the more I think about it, is that these Roads aren't necessary for Transcendence itself, they are philosophies and codes of conduct that prepare a Wraith for a relevant Far Shore. They might push Wraiths to do things that aid in Transcendence, like drop Fetters, and they might have some benefits like bonuses to resolving Passions. Possibly they even constrain Harrowings to match the themes and elements of the Road, though that last part would likely be a real problem as the Far Shores sink into decay. However, they are just helpful to Transcendence, not actually necessary.<br /> <br /> I think its a good fit for Wraith thematically, but I don't think the Road system fits mechanically. It would probably be better to work within the Passions system. By following the path the Wraith builds up a necessary Passion associated with it. Or possibly when a dot of another Passion is resolved, the follower might have the option of instead converting it into the relevant Passion. An associated Dark Passion should be possible as well, but not necessary, so perhaps the player has the option of taking a dot of one instead of any other consequence for a failed Harrowing. Either way, the Passions themselves are the way to track the journey.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}